WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.200
Sizing is refreshingly simple.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.787
Two servers handle up to about
fifty thousand certificates.

3
00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:10.668
Past that, CyberArk's guide splits the
work across six — two each for web, back

4
00:00:10.668 --> 00:00:15.949
end and logging — and beyond a million
certificates CyberArk designs it with you.

5
00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:20.774
For availability, the rules are what you'd
expect: at least two servers per role,

6
00:00:20.774 --> 00:00:23.487
a load balancer in front
of the web services,

7
00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:26.200
and an availability
group for the database.

8
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.200
One nice touch for the certificate
authorities: a CA pool lets the

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.250
platform fail over to a second CA
if the first one stops answering.
